<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:OrdreRas:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Rank of pixel values in a raster</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>This module generates a raster image of indexes according to the order (ascending or descending) that corresponds to the original input raster values.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Rank of pixel values in a raster"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This module generates a raster image of indexes according to the order (ascending or descending) that corresponds to the original input raster values."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Ordre</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Order</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[<li><ul>A. For ascending rank.</li><li>    D.  For descending rank.</li></ul>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Order"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>A</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>D</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>A</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerRAS</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Input raster</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Original raster image file IMG.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:RASFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LIM_INF</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Inferior limit</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Limiting cell values for the ranking. "/LIM_INF=" must be added before the limit value if the user wants to do the ranking on values greater than or equal to the limit value or "/LIM_SUP=" if the user wants to do the ranking on values lesser than or equal to the limit value.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LIM_SUP</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Upper limit</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Limiting cell values for the ranking. "/LIM_SUP=" must be added if the user wants to do the ranking on values lesser than or equal to the limit value.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>LIM_PIX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Pixels Number</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Maximum number of levels desired.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#double">double</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>DESEMPAT_POSICIO</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Draw in position</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If no tied values are desired, /DESEMPAT_POSICIO can be indicated and priority will be given to the cell in the lowest position for the ascending case and in the highest position for the descending case. If the cells are in the same row, priority will be given to the leftmost cell for the ascending case and the far right cell for the descending case. This option provides results such as the Rank module of the Idrisi software.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerOrdenat</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Ordered file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Output file that will contain the cell values ordered according to their original values.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:OrderedFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>